"color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-09-05T05:28:31Z","updated_at":"2025-09-05T09:48:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\niPhone 15 Pro Max iOS 17.1.1 (21B91)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe shader included in the MRP specifies mediump, and I expect it to be computed with half on iOS.\n\n<img width=\"442\" height=\"125\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7ce0d48-e4bb-4c4c-b8f4-31d38a9d02bb\" />\n\nHowever, the generated MSL code looks like this:\n\n<img width=\"398\" height=\"68\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/762cbe98-81c6-498f-b59a-d882be7f36c2\" />\n\nJust before conversion to MSL, I confirmed that the mediump specification is annotated with RelaxedPrecision in SPIR-V.\nHowever, in the generated MSL code, float is used instead of half.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Export an Xcode project for iOS.\n- Build and run it using Xcode, then check the shader code with GPU Frame Capture.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shader-precision.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22165586/shader-precision.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1"